      "title": "Google AI introduces Tool Retrieval in the Gemini API for efficient access",
      "summary": "Google AI announced Tool Retrieval in the Gemini API, now in preview. The feature allows agents to access hundreds of tools while using fewer tokens.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Currently available in preview in the Gemini API",
        "Gives agents access to hundreds of tools",
        "Designed to use fewer tokens during retrieval"
      ],
      "design_implication": "When an agent interface exposes hundreds of potential tools, bloated system prompts and runaway token costs quickly degrade performance and responsiveness. Tool retrieval shifts the interaction pattern from loading every capability upfront to dynamically fetching only what the current user context demands. Start by auditing your agent's system prompt to separate core permanent actions from specialized utility tools that can be lazily loaded on demand.",
      "implication_lens": "capability",
      "visual_need": "illustrate",
